We present explicitly the remainder parts and the Newtonian contributions of the helicity-conserving and helicity-reversing functions in the lab frame. The remainder parts are given in a post-Minkowskian expansion, while the Newtonian contributions are expressed in a resummed form. The resummed expression for the helicity-conserving function is necessary to regulate the forward divergence. We then project the resummed function onto spin-weighted spherical harmonics, perform a Taylor expansion, and compare the results with those from black hole perturbation theory.

